# 16. Final acceptance criteria

The work is not complete until:

- A stale playlist upload cannot resurrect a deleted playlist.
- A publisher cannot publish an incomplete, removed, or stale snapshot.
- Snapshot garbage collection cannot corrupt active or recently published data.
- Independent device edits are not silently discarded.
- Account A data cannot be synchronized into account B.
- Backup restoration cannot leave a partially restored library after a reported failure.
- Artwork removal and replacement have deterministic semantics.
- Long-offline devices cannot silently undo established deletions.
- Incremental synchronization cannot permanently skip records.
- Sign-out and account deletion are safe under timeout, cancellation, and retry.
- Android Keystore instrumentation tests execute successfully on an emulator.
- Firestore security rules and application writes agree.
- Room migrations pass from every supported historical schema.
- Release builds are reproducible, correctly signed when published, and non-debuggable.
- Existing working functionality remains intact.
- All relevant tests pass, or any unverified item is explicitly documented.

